@startuml HermesBaseArch
title Hermes: high-level architecture
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 50
skinparam ranksep 60

package "Client Zone" #FFE5DD {
  component "hermes-cli\nCLI / TUI" as CLI
  component "System editor\nVim / Nano" as Editor
}

package "Server Zone" #E0F4E0 {
  component "hermes-document-service\nUsers / authentication\nWorkspaces / documents" as HDS
  component "hermes-notification-service\nWebSocket connections\nRouting / delivery" as HNS

  database "PostgreSQL\nDomain data\nOwner: document-service" as DomainDB
  database "Redis\nActive sessions" as Redis
  queue "Apache Kafka\nDomain events" as Kafka
  database "PostgreSQL\nDurable inbox\nOwner: notification-service" as InboxDB
}

CLI --> Editor : Run editor
CLI --> HDS : Public API (HTTP / gRPC)\nDomain operations / login / logout
CLI <--> HNS : WebSocket\nConnect / receive messages

HDS --> DomainDB : Read / write domain data
HDS --> Redis : Create / validate / revoke sessions
HNS --> Redis : Validate session
HDS --> Kafka : Publish domain events
Kafka --> HNS : Consume events / fan out
HNS ..> InboxDB : Persist / read inbox\nPolicy under discussion

HDS ..> Redis : Proposed: update user settings\nand publish change signal
Redis ..> HNS : Proposed: settings lookup\nand Pub/Sub updates

legend bottom
  Solid links: accepted architectural direction.
  Dotted links: proposals or policies still under discussion.
  Redis and Kafka are shared contracts; each service owns its PostgreSQL data.
  Authorization distribution and delivery guarantees remain open (arch/notes.txt).
endlegend
@enduml
